      "problem": "Evaluate $\\sinh 1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\sinh x$ is \n\n$$\n\\sinh{x} = \\dfrac{1}{2}(e^{x} - e^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡1 & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{1}-{e}^{-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(e-\\frac{1}{e}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{e}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
